WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.197
The important question is whether the join preserves the measure's fact grain.

00:00:04.197 --> 00:00:08.177
A many-to-one lookup often preserves the fact rows.

00:00:08.177 --> 00:00:12.462
A broad join between two fact-like tables can multiply them.

00:00:12.462 --> 00:00:18.192
If rows are already duplicated before the pivot, the pivot aggregates inflated facts.

00:00:18.192 --> 00:00:21.542
Check row counts and key relationships first.

00:00:21.542 --> 00:00:26.022
Joining detail tables before reshaping can multiply rows.

00:00:26.022 --> 00:00:31.382
If the target is one row per patient or product, summarize each one-to-many source to the target grain

00:00:31.382 --> 00:00:33.772
before combining them.

00:00:33.772 --> 00:00:38.866
This keeps measures interpretable and prevents a pivot from hiding earlier join inflation.
